{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 9,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.671,
            0.049,
            0.846,
            0.067
          ],
          "content": "Finding the Unknown"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.088,
            0.847,
            0.127
          ],
          "content": "Since this action removes the factor 11 in the LHS, we can write this step as:"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.439,
            0.127,
            0.555,
            0.146
          ],
          "content": "y = 66 \\div 11.",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.15,
            0.847,
            0.19
          ],
          "content": "Again, we could have arrived at this by seeing multiplication and division as inverse operations, as in the case of Example 2."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.193,
            0.742,
            0.214
          ],
          "content": "Let us write down both these ways of solving an equation."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.169,
            0.232,
            0.316,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": "11y+(-5)=61",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.504,
            0.232,
            0.651,
            0.253
          ],
          "content": "11y+(-5)=61",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.252,
            0.442,
            0.272
          ],
          "content": "11y+(-5)-(-5)=61-(-5).",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.505,
            0.253,
            0.651,
            0.272
          ],
          "content": "11y = 61 - ( - 5 )",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.17,
            0.271,
            0.255,
            0.29
          ],
          "content": "1 1 y = 6 6",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.505,
            0.271,
            0.592,
            0.291
          ],
          "content": "1 1 y = 6 6",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.169,
            0.29,
            0.341,
            0.309
          ],
          "content": "11y \\div 11 = 66 \\div 11",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.506,
            0.291,
            0.617,
            0.31
          ],
          "content": "y = 66 \\div 11",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.171,
            0.31,
            0.226,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": "y = 6",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.506,
            0.311,
            0.563,
            0.331
          ],
          "content": "y = 6",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.34,
            0.719,
            0.361
          ],
          "content": "Let us consider another equation that we solved earlier."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.38,
            0.325,
            0.4
          ],
          "content": "6y + 7 = 4y + 21",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.511,
            0.38,
            0.66,
            0.4
          ],
          "content": "6y + 7 = 4y + 21",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_17.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.4,
            0.41,
            0.42
          ],
          "content": "6y+7-4y=4y+21-4y",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.511,
            0.4,
            0.66,
            0.419
          ],
          "content": "6y + 7 - 4y = 21",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_19.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.419,
            0.282,
            0.438
          ],
          "content": "2y + 7 = 21",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_20.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.511,
            0.419,
            0.618,
            0.438
          ],
          "content": "2\\bar{y} + 7 = 21",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_21.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.437,
            0.346,
            0.457
          ],
          "content": "2y + 7 - 7 = 21 - 7",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_22.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.51,
            0.438,
            0.617,
            0.457
          ],
          "content": "2y = 21 - 7",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_23.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.457,
            0.254,
            0.476
          ],
          "content": "2 y = 1 4 .",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_24.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.511,
            0.457,
            0.589,
            0.476
          ],
          "content": "2y = 14.",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_25.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.476,
            0.316,
            0.496
          ],
          "content": "2y \\div 2 = 14 \\div 2",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_26.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.512,
            0.476,
            0.614,
            0.496
          ],
          "content": "y = 14 \\div 2",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_27.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.496,
            0.232,
            0.516
          ],
          "content": "y = 7",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_28.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.514,
            0.496,
            0.569,
            0.516
          ],
          "content": "y = 7",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_29.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.54,
            0.493,
            0.573
          ],
          "content": "What happens in cases like $\\frac { u } { 1 5 } = 6 ?$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.576,
            0.715,
            0.598
          ],
          "content": "Multiplying both sides by 15 leaves only u in the LHS —"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.446,
            0.597,
            0.549,
            0.615
          ],
          "content": "u = 6 \\times 15",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_32.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.463,
            0.62,
            0.534,
            0.639
          ],
          "content": "w = 90.",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_33.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.644,
            0.628,
            0.664
          ],
          "content": "Thus, we can make the following observations —"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.669,
            0.847,
            0.746
          ],
          "content": "(a) When a term that is added or subtracted on one side of an equation is removed from that side, its additive inverse should appear as a term on the other side for the equality to hold. For example, $2 y + 7$ = 21 becomes $2 y = 2 1 - 7$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.751,
            0.848,
            0.83
          ],
          "content": "(b) If one side of an equation is the product of two or more numbers or expressions, and we remove one of the factors, then the other side should be divided by this factor for the equality to hold. For example, $2 y = 1 4$ becomes $y = 1 4 \\div 2$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.833,
            0.848,
            0.892
          ],
          "content": "(c) If one side of an equation is the quotient of two numbers or expressions, and we remove the divisor, then the other side should be multiplied by this divisor for the equality to hold. For example,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.195,
            0.895,
            0.446,
            0.928
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{u}{15}=6  becomes   u=6 \\times 15.",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_38.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.806,
            0.932,
            0.846,
            0.95
          ],
          "content": ""
        }
      ]
    }
